# Second-source certificate receipts for the lambda lower bound.
#
# results/strip_mu_certificates.log is the primary log, every row of it taken on
# gympie in July 2026. L3 states 6.543 <= lambda <= 9.3154 and calls both ends
# checkable in exact arithmetic, and the lower end rests on a single receipt:
# mu_17 >= 6543/1000. Until 2026-08-19 that receipt had been produced once, on
# one machine, by a binary built on that machine.
#
# These rows are the same certificates re-derived on ayr (Debian, g++ 12.2)
# from a fresh clone, by scripts/lambda_cert_reproduce.sh, which diffs each
# rational against the primary log and fails closed on any mismatch or on a
# banked row it cannot find. Every one matched, H=17 included.
#
# Two things worth noting from the comparison:
#   - attempts, states and min_ratio agree exactly, and mu_float agrees to all
#     ten printed digits, so the double-precision power iteration is landing on
#     the same value on both machines and not merely a nearby one.
#   - H=17 took 4559 s here against 772.7 s on gympie, a factor of 5.9 in
#     single-thread wall for identical work. That is the machines, not the
#     arithmetic.
#
